  "question": {
    "text": "The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>th</mi></msup></math> roots of unity are in"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AP</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>GP</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HP</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "None of these",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>cos</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>sin</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo></math></p><p>Then, the roots are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo></math>&nbsp;which are clearly on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>GP</mi></math> with common ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></math></p>"
  }
